---
import BaseLayout from '../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';

const privacyEmail = import.meta.env.PUBLIC_PRIVACY_EMAIL?.trim() || 'privacy@anchor.com';
---

<BaseLayout
  title="Terms of use"
  description="Terms of use for the Anchor hackathon prototype."
  currentPath="/terms"
>
  <article class="prose">
    <h1>Terms of use</h1>
    <p class="lede">
      These terms govern use of the Anchor website and bot. Questions:{' '}
      <a href={`mailto:${privacyEmail}`}>{privacyEmail}</a>.
    </p>

    <h2>Prototype status</h2>
    <p>
      Anchor is an OpenConf hackathon prototype. Features may change, break, or lose data. Do not rely on it for clinical
      care or irreversible decisions.
    </p>

    <h2>Sign-in</h2>
    <p>
      You register with an email and a password, and you accept these Terms and the Privacy policy before adding the bot.
      You are responsible for activity under that account and, once you connect a chat, under that connected identity in
      the family group.
    </p>

    <h2>Acceptable use</h2>
    <ul>
      <li>Do not upload unlawful content or others’ personal data without a lawful basis.</li>
      <li>Do not attempt to disrupt the service, scrape aggressively, or bypass security.</li>
      <li>Do not use Anchor to diagnose or treat medical conditions.</li>
    </ul>

    <h2>AI features</h2>
    <p>
      Moment extraction and speech use OpenAI. Outputs can be wrong. You remain responsible for what you share with
      the family chat.
    </p>

    <h2>Intellectual property</h2>
    <p>You retain rights to content you submit. You grant us a licence to process it to provide the service.</p>

    <h2>Liability</h2>
    <p>
      The service is provided “as is” without warranties. To the fullest extent permitted by law we are not liable for
      indirect or consequential loss arising from the prototype.
    </p>

    <h2>Governing law</h2>
    <p>These terms are intended for users in the EU/EEA; mandatory consumer protections still apply where relevant.</p>
  </article>
</BaseLayout>
